@startuml

title Constructor-Based Dependency Injection During Module Loading

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 11

skinparam sequence {
    ParticipantBackgroundColor #F7F7F7
    ParticipantBorderColor #303030
    LifeLineBorderColor #505050
    LifeLineBackgroundColor white
    ArrowColor #202020
    MessageSpacing 34
}

participant ModuleLoader as Loader
participant CommunicatorFactory as Factory
participant "Concrete\nCommunicator" as Concrete
participant CommandHandler as Handler

Loader -> Factory : create_communicator(\ncommMode)
activate Factory

Factory -> Concrete : Instantiate according\nto commMode (NULL, MQTT_PUB, ...)
activate Concrete

Concrete --> Factory : communicator instance
deactivate Concrete

Factory --> Loader : CommunicatorInterface
deactivate Factory

create Handler
Loader -> Handler : CommandHandler(xml_node,\ncommunicator)

note over Loader,Handler
The ModuleLoader reads the communication configuration from the EvaML element, requests
the appropriate communicator from the factory, and injects the CommunicatorInterface into the
CommandHandler constructor.
end note

@enduml